; TEST: expect-exit=100 c-emit-exit=4
;
; `ordinata` over floats: one accumulator started at the op's IDENTITY, each
; `contrib` folding acc = op(acc, v) in contribution order, `redfin` handing
; back acc (ssa-ir.md 2.6, as defined 2026-09-25). Checked as BIT PATTERNS
; through `store f32` / `load u32` (float_mem.ir pins that path), because
; two of the four checks are about a difference `fcmp.eq` cannot see.
;
;   1  fadd f32, contributions [-0.0]        = +0.0    0x00000000
;   2  fsub f32, contributions [1.0, 2.0]    = -3.0    0xC0400000
;   3  fadd f64, contributions [0.5, 0.25]   = 0.75    0x3FE8000000000000
;   4  fmul f32, contributions [3.0, 7.0]    = 21.0    0x41A80000
;
; CHECK 1 IS THE DEFINITION'S SHARPEST EDGE. The identity for `fadd` is
; +0.0, and IEEE says +0.0 + -0.0 is +0.0 -- so a single contribution of
; -0.0 comes back as +0.0, and the SIGN IS GONE. That is the definition and
; not an accident of this lowering: the accumulator exists before any
; contribution does (an empty reduction must answer the identity --
; red_empty.ir), so `redfin` cannot special-case "one contribution, hand it
; back unchanged" without making the answer depend on the count. A lowering
; that started the accumulator AT the first contribution instead of folding
; it would return 0x80000000 here and pass every other check in this
; directory.
;
; CHECK 2 IS WHY `sub` IS IN THE ADDITIVE GROUP. Its identity is 0.0 too, so
; the fold chain is ((0.0 - 1.0) - 2.0) = -3.0, not 1.0 - 2.0 = -1.0. `sub`
; reduces to "negate the sum", which is what folding from the identity
; means; the alternative -- first contribution as the seed -- is a different
; function and is not what spec 5.4's reduction is.
;
; Every figure above is a hand-checkable dyadic rational; the reference that
; produced them is recorded in red_arborea_f32.ir's header (the same
; `ordinata`/`tree`/`arborea` transcription of ssa-ir.md 2.6).
;
; Mutation (run): the accumulator seeded with the first contribution instead
; of the identity -> exit 1 and exit 2 (`fsub` gives -1.0). `fsub`'s
; identity taken as the first operand of a two-operand subtraction -> exit 2.
;
; `c-emit-exit=4`: the C backend refuses the reduction opcodes by name
; (c-backend.md D4 rows 36-38).

functio @initium (ptr) -> u8 {
b0:
%0 = param ptr 0
%1 = slot 8 8
%2 = fconst f32 2147483648
%3 = redinit f32 fadd ordinata 0
contrib %3 %2
%4 = redfin f32 %3
store f32 %1 0 nativus %4
%5 = load u32 %1 0 nativus
%6 = iconst u32 0
%7 = cmp.eq u32 %5 %6
br %7 b2 b1
b1:
%8 = iconst u8 1
ret %8
b2:
%9 = fconst f32 1065353216
%10 = fconst f32 1073741824
%11 = redinit f32 fsub ordinata 0
contrib %11 %9
contrib %11 %10
%12 = redfin f32 %11
store f32 %1 0 nativus %12
%13 = load u32 %1 0 nativus
%14 = iconst u32 3225419776
%15 = cmp.eq u32 %13 %14
br %15 b4 b3
b3:
%16 = iconst u8 2
ret %16
b4:
%17 = fconst f64 4602678819172646912
%18 = fconst f64 4598175219545276416
%19 = redinit f64 fadd ordinata 0
contrib %19 %17
contrib %19 %18
%20 = redfin f64 %19
store f64 %1 0 nativus %20
%21 = load u64 %1 0 nativus
%22 = iconst u64 4604930618986332160
%23 = cmp.eq u64 %21 %22
br %23 b6 b5
b5:
%24 = iconst u8 3
ret %24
b6:
%25 = fconst f32 1077936128
%26 = fconst f32 1088421888
%27 = redinit f32 fmul ordinata 0
contrib %27 %25
contrib %27 %26
%28 = redfin f32 %27
store f32 %1 0 nativus %28
%29 = load u32 %1 0 nativus
%30 = iconst u32 1101529088
%31 = cmp.eq u32 %29 %30
br %31 b8 b7
b7:
%32 = iconst u8 4
ret %32
b8:
%33 = iconst u8 100
ret %33
}
